{
  "abstract": "We prove the following mod-2 identity for real symplectic Banach spaces:\n  If $(X, \\omega)$ is a real symplectic Banach space, and $T \\in L(X)$ satisfies:\n    (1) $I + T^+T$ is Fredholm\n    (2) $I + T^2$ has finite rank\n  Then\n    $\\rank(T^2 + I) \\equiv \\dim \\ker (I + T^+T) \\pmod 2$.\nIn the above, $T^+$ represents the symplectic adjoint. See our paper for more depth in definitions. This identity is applied to show that no hyperplane of the real Kalton-Peck space has a complex structure. We note that in our notation, a symplectic Banach space always assumes that the symplectic form \\omega is a strong symplectic form. See our paper for more detail on the definitions.\nWe formalize:\n (1) The mod-2 identity for arbitrary real symplectic Banach spaces\n (2) An application of the identity to show that if $T \\in L(Z_2)$ and $T^2 + I$ has finite rank, then $T^2 + I$ has even rank.\n     Here, Z_2 is the real Kalton-Peck space.\n (3) The corollary that no hyperplane of the real Kalton-Peck space has a complex structure.",
